## Problem

`updateBookmark` and `deleteBookmark` decide success purely from `resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK`. Pinboard signals write failures **in the response body at HTTP 200**, not via the status line. A failed add returns `<result code="something went wrong"/>` and a delete of an unknown URL returns `<result code="item not found"/>` — both with a 200.

Neither function reads the body at all; both discard it and return nil.</problem>
<parameter name="evidence">main.go:439-443:

```go
if resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {
	return fmt.Errorf("update failed: %d", resp.StatusCode)
}

return nil
```

main.go:464-468 (identical shape in `deleteBookmark`):

```go
if resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {
	return fmt.Errorf("delete failed: %d", resp.StatusCode)
}

return nil
```

Pinboard API documentation, `posts/add`:

> If the post was successful: `<result code="done" />`
> If the post failed: `<result code="something went wrong" />`

Pinboard API documentation, Differences From Delicious API:

> `posts/delete` returns `<result code="item not found" />` if the user does not have that URL in their bookmarks.

The nil return then drives the counters, main.go:283-285 and main.go:321:

```go
} else if err == nil {
	stats.IncrementUpdates()
}
...
stats.IncrementDeletions()
```

Neither request sends `format=json`, so the body is XML in any case.</evidence>
<parameter name="impact">Every write failure Pinboard reports in-band is recorded as a success. The end-of-run statistics report "Updates performed" and "Deletions performed" counts that overstate what actually changed, and the operator receives no signal that anything went wrong — a tag list over the 100-tag limit, a title over 255 characters, or a URL scheme Pinboard rejects all silently no-op while being reported as applied. Combined with the missing 429 handling, a rate-limited run can report a full set of successful updates having performed none.</impact>
<parameter name="fix">Request JSON and check the result code in both functions.

- Append `&format=json` to the `posts/add` and `posts/delete` query strings.
- Decode `struct{ ResultCode string \`json:"result_code"\` }` and return an error unless `ResultCode == "done"`:

```go
var result struct {
	ResultCode string `json:"result_code"`
}
if err := json.NewDecoder(resp.Body).Decode(&result); err != nil {
	return fmt.Errorf("failed to decode Pinboard write result: %w", err)
}
if result.ResultCode != "done" {
	return fmt.Errorf("pinboard rejected the write: %s", result.ResultCode)
}
```

- Keep the existing status-code check ahead of the decode so a 429 or 5xx still short-circuits.

Extend `TestUpdateBookmark_Error` and `TestDeleteBookmark_Error` with a case that returns HTTP 200 and `{"result_code":"something went wrong"}`, asserting a non-nil error. Those tests currently only cover the 401 path, which is why this gap survived.</fix>
</invoke>

